# Kinetic design record — Petit Jour, parent app, home screen "Aujourd'hui".
kdl: 1
mode: create

product:
  name: Petit Jour
  stack: react-native
  platforms: [ios, android]
  users: parents of children aged 3 months to 3 years in a small network of French crèches; often anxious, especially in the first months; carers are professionals who log the day on a shared tablet
  moment: at work between two meetings, phone in one hand, 3 to 10 seconds ("is she napping? did she eat?"); again at pick-up time on the pavement; and when a notification says something needs them
  frequency: daily
  stakes: medium
  density: medium
  brand:
    status: none
    colors: []
    fonts: []
  facts:
    - interface language is French
    - carers log arrival, meals with quantity (all, half, a little, refused), naps (start and end), nappies, moments with an occasional photo, temperature and health notes, with author and time
    - pending things exist - unread carer message, document to sign, item to bring, planned absence, pick-up time and person
    - logs can lag by up to an hour; network can be offline
    - a fever of 38 °C or more means the parent must call the crèche
    - some families have two children in the same crèche
  unknowns:
    - whether carers can mark a note as urgent themselves (assumed - the fever rule is computed, other notes are not escalated)
    - whether the parent can edit the pick-up person from the app or only notify (assumed - notify, carers confirm)

requirements:
  - {id: R1, need: know what the child is doing right now and when it was logged, priority: must, above_fold: true, element: now-card}
  - {id: R2, need: see whether she ate and slept today without reading the whole day, priority: must, above_fold: true, element: day-brief}
  - {id: R3, need: see everything the crèche is waiting for from me (message, signature, item to bring), priority: must, above_fold: true, element: for-you}
  - {id: R4, need: read the day as logged by carers - arrival, meals with quantity, naps, nappies, moments with photo, health notes, author and time, priority: must, element: day-thread}
  - {id: R5, need: know pick-up time and who picks up, change it, priority: must, above_fold: true, element: pickup-row}
  - {id: R6, need: an important health note (fever 38 °C or more) is impossible to miss and leads to a call, priority: must, above_fold: true, element: health-alert}
  - {id: R7, need: switch between two children in the same crèche, priority: must, element: child-switch}
  - {id: R8, need: day states - not arrived yet, absent today, day over, crèche closed, priority: must, element: now-card}
  - {id: R9, need: honest about lag and offline - say when the last note was written and when data was received, priority: must, element: freshness}
  - {id: R10, need: declare an absence or a delay, priority: should, element: absence-link}
  - {id: R11, need: reach the crèche by phone at any time, priority: should, element: call-button}

thesis:
  statement: The glance a parent takes between two meetings to know what their child is doing right now and what the crèche needs from them, told the way a carer would tell it at the door.
  feel: [reassured, informed, held]
  never: [a metrics dashboard of a toddler, a social feed to scroll, a hospital alarm for ordinary notes, a to-do list that makes parents feel guilty]
  spine: her day as one thread of light, from arrival to now
  spine_expressions:
    layout: one vertical thread with the present at its head (a sentence, not a number) and the arrival at its foot; everything else hangs off it or sits above it as "pour vous"
    color: the head of the thread takes the light of her moment - warm daylight when she is awake, dusk blue while she naps, neutral when she is home or the crèche is closed; red exists only for the fever rule
    motion: only what is happening now moves (the live node breathes slowly during an ongoing nap); logged moments stay still
  because: parents asked for presence and reassurance, not performance; a carer at the door speaks in sentences and in order

expression:
  level: 2
  because: health-adjacent and anxious users cap expression; daily glance use favours precision; identity lives in one serif sentence and in the light of the now-card
  factors: {stakes: medium, frequency: daily, density: medium, brand_freedom: high}

directions:
  - id: A
    name: Cahier de liaison
    axes: {structure: single column narrative - a now sentence then requests then a bounded thread, density: balanced, color: warm paper neutrals with one ink-green accent and a state-driven light on the now card, type: serif sentence for the present and SF text for everything else, motion: still and native calm with one live breath}
    scores: {product_fit: 5, distinctiveness: 4, usability: 5, feasibility: 5, risk_of_slop: 2}
    verdict: chosen
    because: mirrors the paper liaison notebook French crèches already use; answers the glance in a sentence; the bounded thread (arrival to now) cannot become an endless feed
  - id: B
    name: Tableau de bord du jour
    axes: {structure: hub of status tiles with a horizontal day ribbon 7 h 30 to 18 h 30, density: dense, color: neutral grey with one signal colour per category, type: grotesk tabular numerals, motion: precise ticks on update}
    scores: {product_fit: 2, distinctiveness: 3, usability: 4, feasibility: 4, risk_of_slop: 4}
    verdict: rejected
    because: turns a toddler's day into tiles and counters - exactly thesis.never (metrics dashboard, D04); the ribbon needs a legend (D31)
  - id: C
    name: Fil de la section
    axes: {structure: chat-like feed of carer posts and photos newest first, density: airy, color: dominant brand surface with photo-led cards, type: rounded friendly display, motion: lively entrances on new posts}
    scores: {product_fit: 2, distinctiveness: 3, usability: 3, feasibility: 3, risk_of_slop: 4}
    verdict: rejected
    because: a social network to scroll (thesis.never); photo-first ranking rewards the occasional photo over the meal and the nap that parents actually check

journeys:
  - id: midday-glance
    steps:
      - {screen: today, intent: between meetings - is she napping, did she eat, risk: answer below the fold or buried in a feed}
      - {screen: today, intent: see a message from Inès is waiting, risk: message lost among day entries}
  - id: fever-call
    steps:
      - {screen: today, intent: notification - temperature logged at 38.4 °C, risk: alert reads as an ordinary note or panics with alarm styling everywhere}
      - {screen: today, intent: call the crèche in one tap, risk: phone number hidden in a profile screen}
  - id: pick-up
    steps:
      - {screen: today, intent: on the pavement - when and who picks up, change it to the grandmother, risk: pick-up info only in a settings screen}
      - {screen: today, intent: after pick-up read the end-of-day word, risk: day over looks like an error or empty screen}

system:
  type:
    families: {display: New York (ui-serif) / Noto Serif on Android, text: SF Pro / Roboto (system)}
    scale:
      display: {size: 28, line: 34, weight: 400, track: -0.01}
      title: {size: 20, line: 25, weight: 600, track: -0.01}
      headline: {size: 17, line: 22, weight: 600, track: 0}
      body: {size: 17, line: 24, weight: 400, track: 0}
      callout: {size: 15, line: 20, weight: 400, track: 0}
      footnote: {size: 13, line: 18, weight: 400, track: 0, numerals: tabular}
      tab: {size: 11, line: 13, weight: 500, track: 0.01}
    dynamic: true
  color:
    seed: "#2B6555"
    strategy: neutral+accent
    roles:
      light:
        bg: "#F6F2EB"
        surface: "#FFFDF9"
        surface-2: "#EEE8DE"
        border: "#E3DBCF"
        text: "#22201C"
        text-2: "#5F5A52"
        text-3: "#8A847A"
        accent: "#2B6555"
        on-accent: "#FFFFFF"
        danger: "#B3261E"
        on-danger: "#FFFFFF"
      dark:
        bg: "#13120F"
        surface: "#1D1B18"
        surface-2: "#27241F"
        border: "#35312B"
        text: "#EEE9E1"
        text-2: "#ABA398"
        text-3: "#7D776E"
        accent: "#8CC2B0"
        on-accent: "#0B2019"
        danger: "#F2A59C"
        on-danger: "#1F1210"
    data:
      daylight: {light: "#F8E9D6", dark: "#2A2219", on: "#22201C", on_dark: "#EEE9E1"}
      dusk: {light: "#E6E8F2", dark: "#1E2130", on: "#22201C", on_dark: "#EEE9E1"}
      alert: {light: "#FBE4E0", dark: "#3A1A16", on: "#22201C", on_dark: "#EEE9E1"}
  space:
    unit: 4
    scale: {xs: 4, s: 8, m: 12, l: 16, xl: 24, 2xl: 32, 3xl: 48}
    margins: {compact: 20, regular: 24}
  shape:
    corner: continuous
    radius: {s: 8, m: 12, l: 20, full: 999}
  elevation:
    strategy: tonal
  icon:
    family: custom
    style: outline
    selected: fill
    sizes: [20, 24]
    weight: 1.75 stroke on a 24 grid, round caps and joins
  motion:
    personality: native calm - critically damped, short, nothing bounces; only the live node breathes
    springs:
      settle: {response: 0.4, damping: 1.0}
      press: {response: 0.25, damping: 1.0}
    durations: {quick: 150, standard: 220, breath: 1200}
    reduce: crossfade
  haptics:
    select: selection
    confirm: soft
    alert: warning

screens:
  - id: today
    job: tell a parent in one glance what their child is doing now, whether she ate and slept, and what the crèche needs from them
    serves: [R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R6, R7, R8, R9, R10, R11]
    thumb: [tab bar, for-you rows, pickup change, absence link]
    network: true
    primary: the now sentence in serif on the lit now card (e.g. "Léa fait la sieste depuis 13 h 05")
    secondary: the day brief under it (meal, sleep, nappies in words) and the pick-up row
    reading_order: [health-alert, now-card, day-brief, for-you, day-thread, absence-link]   # pickup-row sits inside the now card, under the brief
    components:
      - id: child-switch
        kind: tab
        role: two children - name plus their current state in words, one selected
        fg: $color.text
        bg: $color.surface
        target: 44
        variants: [default, pressed, selected, disabled]
        haptic: $haptic.select
        env: {on: $color.bg, near: [now-card], zone: top - acceptable because it is a rare switch, density: low}
      - id: call-button
        kind: icon-button
        role: call the crèche from anywhere
        fg: $color.accent
        bg: $color.bg
        target: 44
        variants: [default, pressed, disabled]
      - id: now-card
        kind: card
        role: the head of the thread - one serif sentence, time logged, author
        fg: $color.text
        bg: $color.surface
        env: {on: $color.bg, near: [day-brief, pickup-row], density: low}
      - id: now-sentence
        kind: text
        type: $type.display
        fg: $color.text
        bg: $color.surface
      - id: pickup-row
        kind: row
        role: pick-up time and person, Modifier action
        fg: $color.text
        bg: $color.surface
        target: 44
        variants: [default, pressed, disabled]
      - id: health-alert
        kind: card
        role: fever 38 °C or more - one sentence, who measured it and when, call action
        fg: $color.text
        bg: $color.surface
      - id: call-crèche-button
        kind: button
        fg: $color.on-danger
        bg: $color.danger
        target: 48
        variants: [default, pressed, disabled]
        haptic: $haptic.alert
      - id: for-you-row
        kind: row
        role: one thing the crèche waits for - message, signature, item, with due date
        fg: $color.text
        bg: $color.surface
        target: 56
        variants: [default, pressed, disabled, loading]
      - id: day-thread
        kind: list
        role: the day as logged - newest at the top, arrival at the foot; time, what, detail, author
        env: {on: $color.bg, near: [for-you], density: medium}
      - id: thread-time
        kind: text
        type: $type.footnote
        fg: $color.text-2
        bg: $color.bg
      - id: absence-link
        kind: link
        fg: $color.accent
        bg: $color.bg
        target: 44
        variants: [default, pressed, disabled]
      - id: tab-bar
        kind: tab-bar
        fg: $color.text-2
        bg: $color.surface
    states:
      content: nap in progress at 14 h 20 - dusk-lit now card, brief (déjeuner la moitié, 2 changes), pick-up 17 h 30 with Marc, three things for you, thread from sieste back to arrival
      loading: first open without cache - header with the child name (known locally), now card and thread in quiet skeletons with "Chargement de la journée de Léa…"; with cache the previous day content stays and only the freshness line updates
      empty: arrived but nothing logged yet - "Arrivée à 8 h 40" then "Les notes de l'équipe apparaîtront ici au fil de la journée"; not-arrived, absent and closed are designed day states, never empty screens
      error: day could not be loaded - plain cause, Réessayer, and the phone number of the crèche as the fallback that always works
      offline: cached day stays readable; banner "Hors ligne" (no time); the time is said once, in the now-card kicker "reçu à 14 h 02"; live durations and the breathing dot stop, the sentence switches to past tense ("faisait la sieste"); a signature done offline shows "Envoi en attente du réseau"
      stale: logs lag - "Dernière note à 11 h 45" stated on the now card, the sentence is written as the last known fact with its time, and a one-line explanation that carers often write after meals and naps
      partial: photo failed to load - frame keeps its size with "Photo indisponible", text of the moment stays
      overflow: long French strings and relations ("grand-mère, personne autorisée") wrap; times are glued with no-break spaces ("depuis 13 h 05" never splits); two naps stack one per line; from about XXXL text the pick-up "Modifier" moves under the text (gallery texte-tres-grand renders ×1.35); only the message preview is clamped to 2 lines (full text one tap away)
      first-run: n/a: onboarding and account linking are a separate flow; the home starts with a linked child
    motion:
      - id: live-breath
        kind: signature
        trigger: an ongoing nap is shown on the now card and at the head of the thread
        change: the live dot fades 1.0 to 0.35 and back, 1.2 s each way, nothing else moves
        duration: $duration.breath
        reduce: static dot, no animation, the word "en cours" carries the state
        interruptible: true
      - id: child-switch-crossfade
        kind: transition
        trigger: parent selects the other child
        change: content below the switch crossfades (opacity 0 to 1, 4 pt rise) in 220 ms
        duration: $duration.standard
        reduce: crossfade without the rise
        interruptible: true
      - id: press
        kind: feedback
        trigger: press on any row, link or button
        change: opacity 0.6 within 100 ms, back on release
        duration: $duration.quick
        reduce: same, opacity is not motion
        interruptible: true

signature:
  what: the now card is the lit head of the day thread - one serif sentence about her present moment, lit in warm daylight when she is awake and dusk blue while she naps, with a slowly breathing live dot only while something is in progress; the thread nodes below carry the same two lights (dusk for naps, daylight for waking moments)
  where: [today]
  because: makes the spine (her day as one thread of light) literal; the parent reads the state from the words and feels it from the light, without a number or a legend

premortem:
  - risk: warm paper plus serif reads as a lifestyle or wedding app rather than a trustworthy crèche tool
    rule: D14
    fix: serif only for the one present-tense sentence; everything else system sans, tabular times, plain labels
  - risk: the day brief becomes a row of counters (2 changes, 45 min) - a dashboard costume
    rule: D04
    fix: brief in words ("a mangé la moitié", "sieste en cours"), no rings, no totals beyond nappies
  - risk: fever alert, unread message, signature and item all styled urgent - everything shouts
    rule: D32
    fix: red only for the fever rule; for-you rows share one quiet style with due dates in words; unread is a dot plus the word "non lu" for screen readers
  - risk: the thread turns into a feed that parents scroll anxiously for updates
    rule: D18
    fix: bounded thread (arrival at the foot, no infinite load), no entrance animations, freshness stated once on the now card
  - risk: lag is hidden - "fait la sieste" stated in present tense when the last note is an hour old
    rule: F01
    fix: sentence tense follows freshness; stale and offline states write the last known fact with its time
